# Printer Setup: writes each fabricator's device IDs into Printer Control's stack, then
# ends. d0: Printer Control's housing. Stack 0: how many fabricators; then 12 slots each.
# In a block, slot 6 is unused (Control reads the input amount from slot 10), and Control
# writes slots 11 and 12 itself.
alias Memory d0

put Memory 0 3 # number of fabricators

# Fabricator 1 (Autolathe 1): slots 1-12
put Memory 1 $1488 # Printer
put Memory 2 $3606 # Stacker
put Memory 3 $AE16A # Progress display
put Memory 4 $AE19B # Amount display
put Memory 5 $AE87A # Power input
put Memory 6 $AEF03 # Input amount (unused)
put Memory 7 $AE0D8 # Input stack toggle
put Memory 8 $AEEEA # Plus 10 button
put Memory 9 $AEEF9 # Minus 10 button
put Memory 10 $AEF03  # Input amount
put Memory 11 0     # Selected Amount
put Memory 12 0     # Reserve for productionMode

# Fabricator 2 (Electronics 1): slots 13-24
put Memory 13 $2736 # Printer
put Memory 14 $360F # Stacker
put Memory 15 $C3042 # Progress display
put Memory 16 $C3007 # Amount display
put Memory 17 797452 # Power input
put Memory 18 $C2AB1 # Input amount (unused)
put Memory 19 $C2AF0 # Input stack toggle
put Memory 20 $C2A6A # Plus 10 button
put Memory 21 $C2A6F # Minus 10 button
put Memory 22 $C2AB1 # Input amount
put Memory 23 0     # Selected Amount
put Memory 24 0     # Reserve for productionMode

# Fabricator 3 (Pipe Bender 1): slots 25-36
put Memory 25 $2217 # Printer
put Memory 26 $3607 # Stacker
put Memory 27 $C3D42 # Progress display
put Memory 28 $C5295 # Amount display
put Memory 29 802081 # Power input
put Memory 30 $C3D17 # Input amount (unused)
put Memory 31 $C3D27 # Input stack toggle
put Memory 32 $C3CF5 # Plus 10 button
put Memory 33 $C3CFA # Minus 10 button
put Memory 34 $C3D17 # Input amount
put Memory 35 0     # Selected Amount
put Memory 36 0     # Reserve for productionMode

# Another fabricator: uncomment, set its IDs, and make the count at the top 4.
#put Memory 37 $0 # Printer
#put Memory 38 $0 # Stacker
